// Package @{.Name}@ is the @{.Name}@ connector: it lets Chaperone act on one
// service for an agent, so the agent never holds a credential for it.
//
// This package was written by `go run ./internal/connectors/scaffold @{.Name}@`
// and is not registered anywhere: chapd does not build its adapters, the
// catalog does not list its operations and the baseline does not name them.
// docs/write-a-connector.md says what to write and which steps are done by
// hand.
//
// What is where:
//
//   - @{.Name}@spec/spec.go declares the operations once (name, class,
//     reversibility, usage, rate, target, params). Replace the example.
//   - adapter.go holds the adapters: Check and Execute of each operation. The
//     two of the example refuse until they are written.
//   - client.go is a small HTTP client that sends the credential in one header
//     and never puts it, or the service's error text, in an error.
//   - @{.Name}@test/server.go is a fake of the service for the tests.
//   - conformance_test.go runs the shared connector suite
//     (internal/connectors/conformance) against the real adapters and the
//     fake.
package @{.Name}@
